    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>docs/architecture/firestore-sync-backup.md — Firestore sync/backup architecture (post-cleanup)</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Explanation doc covering: single-source collection constants (companion on FirestoreBackupService), <code>withAuthenticatedUser{}</code> guard (FBS only — FSM uses an intentionally distinct early-return guard), <code>addArticleToBatch</code> write helper, <code>applyRemoteArticles</code> restore-loop helper, streamed restore memory contract (<code>suspend onPage</code> callback, <code>Result&lt;Unit&gt;</code>), A2b large-text rehydration parity, batched-tag-read client-only approach, and FTS sanitization fix + result-set impact.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "add", "text": "## Collection layout" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "All path strings are constants in `FirestoreBackupService.companion`." },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "## Streamed restore — memory contract" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "suspend fun restoreAllArticlesPaginated(onProgress, onPage): Result<Unit>" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  // onPage called per page; no list accumulation; restoreAllArticles() removed" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "## FTS search fix" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  // sanitizedQuery (not raw query) now reaches the DAO" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>docs/architecture/app-scope-di.md — App-scope &amp; DI conventions</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Explanation doc covering: the <code>@ApplicationScope @Singleton CoroutineScope(SupervisorJob()+ioDispatcher)</code> pattern provided by <code>AppScopeModule</code>; when to use it vs <code>viewModelScope</code>; why bare <code>CoroutineScope(dispatcher)</code> is a reliability bug (first child exception permanently cancels the scope); why <code>cleanup()</code> must not cancel a singleton scope.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "add", "text": "## The @ApplicationScope scope" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  @Provides @Singleton @ApplicationScope" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  fun provideApplicationScope(...) = CoroutineScope(SupervisorJob() + ioDispatcher)" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "## When to use @ApplicationScope vs viewModelScope" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  // viewModelScope → UI/ViewModel lifecycle; @ApplicationScope → background sync" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "## Anti-pattern: bare CoroutineScope(dispatcher)" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  // First child exception cancels the scope permanently — inject @ApplicationScope instead" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>docs/architecture/batched-tag-reads.md — Batched tag read reference note</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Reference note: <code>batchRestoreArticleTags(articleIds)</code> query shape — subcollection reads dispatched in parallel chunks of <code>RESTORE_TAG_CHUNK_SIZE=10</code> via <code>coroutineScope+async+awaitAll</code>. Includes rationale for rejecting collectionGroup (no <code>userId</code> field on <code>ArticleTags</code>; no <code>firestore.indexes.json</code>; schema migration out of scope). No index deployed, no rules change.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "add", "text": "## Query shape" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  users/{uid}/articles/{articleId}/tags/  (full subcollection get)" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  chunked(RESTORE_TAG_CHUNK_SIZE=10) → coroutineScope { async }.awaitAll()" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "## Why not collectionGroup" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  // ArticleTags has no userId field → cross-user isolation impossible" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  // No firestore.indexes.json; schema migration out of scope" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>README.md — one-line FTS + restore capability note</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Add one sentence to the Android client row: corrected FTS results (sanitized query reaches the DAO) and memory-bounded page-by-page restore (no OOM on large libraries).</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
